3. Governing law: changed from California to Delaware, matching Tessera's other agreements. If Pinewood insists on California we can live with it.
4. Added a carve-out allowing Tessera to disclose the existence of the relationship to investors under their own confidentiality obligations.

Everything else is as Pinewood sent it. If they push back on any of the four, send me their comments and I will turn them the same day.

